Title: Incomplete Remediation: Publicly Disclosed AWS Credentials remain Active, allowing Unauthorized Data Injection into Kinesis Firehose

Summary
While reviewing a publicly disclosed vulnerability on your program (https://hackerone.com/reports/2914739), I discovered that the sensitive AWS credentials mentioned in that report were never revoked. Although the information is now public, the keys remain Active and functional.
I have verified that these credentials still allow unauthorized parties to interact with your AWS infrastructure, specifically the plesk-18.0-ux Firehose stream. This represents a significant security regression and a failure in the remediation process.

